    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **55 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customer-code de-duplication in `ClinicServiceImpl.generateCustomerCode`.\n\nThe existing code built the customer code as `<REGION>-<HASH8>`. I split that into a base value and added a `deduplicateCustomerCode` step:\n\n```java\nprivate String generateCustomerCode(Owner owner) {\n    String base = regionFor(owner) + \"-\" + hash8(owner);\n    return deduplicateCustomerCode(base);\n}\n\nprivate String deduplicateCustomerCode(String base) {\n    Set<String> existing = ownerRepository.findAll().stream()\n        .map(Owner::getCustomerCode)\n        .filter(code -> code != null)\n        .collect(java.util.stream.Collectors.toSet());\n    if (!existing.contains(base)) {\n        return base;\n    }\n    int n = 2;\n    while (existing.contains(base + \"-\" + n)) {\n        n++;\n    }\n    return base + \"-\" + n;\n}\n```\n\nWhen the computed code collides with an existing owner's `customerCode`, it appends `-<n>` with the smallest `n \u2265 2` that yields a code not already in use, and returns that de-duplicated code. When there's no collision, the base code is returned unchanged. This runs before the owner is persisted (in `saveOwner`), consistent with the other pre-persist derivations.",
